tmux with everything removed except tabs. for running coding agents and ssh work.

no prefix key, no panes, no copy mode. chrome shortcuts with ⌥ instead of ⌘:

    ⌥T        new tab (pick claude / codex / pi / opencode / shell)
    ⌥W        close tab
    ⌥⇥ ⌥⇧⇥    next / previous tab

install:

    $ mkdir -p ~/.local/bin
    $ curl -o ~/.local/bin/tabs https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sueszli/tmux-tabs/master/tmux-tabs.sh
    $ chmod +x ~/.local/bin/tabs

usage:

    $ tabs

closing the terminal window leaves the agents running. `tabs` reattaches.
tabs close themselves when the agent exits. runs on its own tmux socket, your
~/.tmux.conf is untouched.

on macOS terminal.app the first run creates a "tmux-tabs" profile (your default
theme + "use option as meta key", otherwise ⌥T would type †) and opens a window
with it. ⌘ itself can't be remapped in terminal.app, hence ⌥.
